{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both fixes are in one commit, `7aaa7d8` (\"Invite preview: canonical origin + always 1200x630 card\"), pushed to `cursor/photo-fixes`, so [PR #14](https://github.com/rept0rix/kiss/pull/14) now includes it. Typecheck, `vite build` (with `DATABASE_URL` unset) and the TypeScript tests (38/38) pass. I didn't merge, deploy, change env vars or touch a real database.\n\n**1) Share origin.** The logic now lives in one small pure helper, `resolveShareOrigin` in `src/lib/share-origin.ts`. `getShareOrigin` calls it, which is what `k.$from.tsx` uses for `og:url` and `og:image`.\n- **Vercel previews** (`VERCEL_ENV` set and not `production`): `VITE_PUBLIC_HOSTNAME` is ignored and the request host is used, so previews point at themselves.\n- **Production:** a `*.vercel.app` hostname, whether pinned or from the request, becomes `https://app.sendkiss.online`. Link previews get no redirect, even before you change the env var.\n- **Off Vercel:** behaviour is unchanged.\n- **`scripts/grok-pwa-shared.mjs`:** left alone. It already refuses any `*.vercel.app` host for og tags, so it can never emit the redirecting one. `/k/` pages also keep their own og tags through `server/lib/share-aware-head.mjs`.\n- Added `src/lib/share-origin.test.ts` (5 cases) to `npm test`.\n\n**2) Card size.** `/c/<code>` and the duplicate `/api/og/<code>` now always return a 1200×630 `image/jpeg`. The new renderer is `src/lib/kisses/share-card-image.ts`, using `sharp` 0.34 and copying the browser card's layout. What it returns depends on what's stored:\n- **Stored card that's already a 1200×630 JPEG:** served as-is.\n- **Stored card with the right shape but the wrong size:** resized.\n- **Anything else, including the 512×512 profile photo:** the photo is cropped into the red-ringed circle on the dark card with \"COME GET IT\".\n- **No photo:** Latin initials are shown. Names without Latin letters, such as Hebrew names, get a lips mark instead, because I only pre-drew glyphs for A–Z and 0–9.\n- **Unknown code:** a generic card instead of a redirect.\n\nVercel's Node functions have no system fonts, so SVG text would render as empty boxes. I turned the card text into drawn shapes ahead of time from the Archivo Black font (free licence) and saved them in `card-glyphs.ts`. Nothing needs a font at runtime.\n\nThe build keeps `sharp` as an external package with its native binary copied into the Vercel function. The lockfile includes the Linux x64 binaries Vercel's build will install. `sharp` stays out of the browser bundle because it's only loaded dynamically from the server route handlers.\n\n**Caching, with no schema change:**\n- **Send-sheet links:** the rendered card is written into the existing `share_cards.body`. In my local test the second request took 4–8 ms instead of 60–160 ms, and it's served with `max-age=86400, s-maxage=604800`.\n- **QR links:** deliberately not stored, since the owner's photo can change. They rely on HTTP caching (1 hour, plus `stale-while-revalidate`). That server-side render is what fixes the QR path, so I didn't add a browser-side card build there.\n\n**Local test:** I ran the dev server on port 8093 with in-memory PGLite and created links through the real `createShareLink` call. Three cases came back 200 as 1200×630 JPEGs:\n- a link with no stored card;\n- a link whose stored \"card\" was a square PNG, which came back framed as a proper card;\n- an unknown code.\n\nI also checked the rendered images by eye.\n\n**Still unchecked:** the new mapping of `*.vercel.app` to `app.sendkiss.online` in production is only covered by the unit tests, not by a real Vercel deployment.\n\n`android/`, `ios/` and the `docs/AGENT-PROMPT-PHOTOS*.txt` files were not committed."}]},"session_id":"1061a2f3-4cc0-419f-bf35-8615ea89d6ea","model_call_id":"5369bd5c-a962-477b-a6db-501249451105-0-xqcf","timestamp_ms":1790667271013}
